This is a copy of a letter that I just finished sending to the dev team.

Some of you may find it informative, and I would like to hear comments
on the three named possible bugs.

---- Begin quoted text
To: nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu
Subject: possible bug w/ cursed items, some comments.


My wizard was wandering through the dungeon the othr day wielding
his cursed samurai sword, when he happened to go downstairs while
carrying a little too much.
A message similar to:
"Your cursed samurai sword follows you down!" appeared,
and I was releived of this burden, which remained lying at the
foot of the stairs.

Is this intentional?  It seems to me that cursed-ness shouldn't
be so easily foiled.




Now on to the comments.
	This entire line of sight algorithm thing should
be taken out back and shot.

	Same for the idea of corpses remaining on the map until
you walk past them again.



Oh!  reminder of a second bug.

	When reading an identify scroll, I was prompted
for what I wished to identify: ([!+=?)... a).
Hitting "a" re-identified my athame.  brilliant way to waste a
scroll.  This is absolutely _NOT_ what I would expect "a" to do.
It should wander through the list, asking me items as it comes to them,
or else just wander through the list identifying things that aren't.



More comments:
	Kudos for finally making rustproofing wishable.

	The idea of spells fading from your memory as you cast them
should be taken out and shot.  What the hell do you think you have
magic points for?  Up the price or lower the regeneration rate...

	Also -- a ring of regenerate magic would be a nifty item.



Third possible bug.
	I found an ice box in the dungeon the other day.
After taking out about 15 corpses of various creatures, I became
"Overburdened".  This not being a really desirable state of affairs, I 
decided to put some of them back.
	as soon as I pressed the key for the corpse I had selected to
place into the icebox, the prompt was gone.  I had to go through the
entire:  #loot, there is an icebox here, loot it? yes, do you
want to take something out? no, do you want to put something in? yes
procedure for each of the corpses in my belongings.  This doesn't seem
right.

	Also, after I had replaced _ALL_ the corpses I had originally taken
out, I was still noted as being "Overburdened".  Moving a couple of places
away and picking up the gold that was there re-set my state to normal,
but this _should_ have happened as I placed the corpses into the icebox.




	This is getting rather long, so I'll let you digest and respond
as you will.  Danke.
